---
import '../../styles/kit.css';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { href, pageMeta } from '../../lib/site';
import { docsArticle, docsBreadcrumbs } from '../../lib/jsonld';
const h1 = "GitHub Action guide";
const wf = "name: a11ign\n\non:\n  pull_request:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n\njobs:\n  a11ign:\n    runs-on: windows-2022\n    timeout-minutes: 20\n    permissions:\n      contents: read\n      pull-requests: write\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v7\n      - uses: a11ign/a11ign@<full-40-character-commit>\n        id: a11ign\n        with:\n          url: https://example.com/contact\n          task: Send an enquiry\n      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v7\n        if: always() && steps.a11ign.outputs.result-json != ''\n        with:\n          name: a11ign-result\n          path: |\n            ${{ steps.a11ign.outputs.result-json }}\n            ${{ steps.a11ign.outputs.summary-md }}";
---

<Page path="/docs/github-action" ogType="article" jsonLd={[docsArticle(h1, pageMeta('/docs/github-action').description, '/docs/github-action'), docsBreadcrumbs(h1, '/docs/github-action')]}>
	<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
	    <div class="bd first"><div class="wrap"><h1 class="t60">GitHub Action guide</h1></div><div class="wrap"><p class="lead" style="margin:16px 0 0">A step-by-step guide to adding a11ign to a GitHub workflow: the workflow file, every setting, and what you get back.</p></div></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="d0" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h2 id="d0" class="t28">What this does</h2></div>
	<p>a11ign runs in GitHub and puts its report on your pull request. <span class="hl">You don’t need a machine of your own, an account or an API key.</span></p>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="d1" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h2 id="d1" class="t28">Add it</h2></div>
	<CodeBlock label={".github/workflows/a11ign.yml"} code={wf} /><ol class="stp"><li><span class="n">1</span><span><b>Save the file</b> as .github/workflows/a11ign.yml.</span></li><li><span class="n">2</span><span><b>Pin a11ign</b> by its full 40-character commit, not a tag or branch, so a new release never changes your build unasked.</span></li><li><span class="n">3</span><span><b>Open a pull request.</b> The report appears as a comment. To find the latest release, run git ls-remote https://github.com/a11ign/a11ign "refs/tags/a11ign@*".</span></li></ol>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="d2" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h2 id="d2" class="t28">Settings you’ll use</h2></div>
	<ul class="sets"><li><div class="set"><code>url</code><p>The page to test.</p><span class="def">Required</span></div></li><li><div class="set"><code>urls</code><p>Several pages, one per line. More than 5 needs max-pages, up to 25.</p></div></li><li><div class="set"><code>task</code><p>A label for the run. It also names the button the optional form check presses.</p><span class="def">Default: Read and understand this page</span></div></li><li><div class="set"><code>fail-on</code><p>Fail the build on findings: never, any, blocker, serious, moderate or minor. Findings marked referred never count.</p><span class="def">Default: never</span></div></li><li><div class="set"><code>probe-forms</code><p>Submits forms with no valid input to hear whether errors are announced, and presses the button your task names. Use it only on a test app.</p><span class="def">Default: off</span></div></li><li><div class="set"><code>comment-on-pr</code><p>Posts the report as a pull request comment, and updates it on later runs.</p><span class="def">Default: on</span></div></li><li><div class="set"><code>judge-backend</code><p>Who judges the transcript. The default is a11ign’s own model, which sends nothing anywhere.</p><span class="def">Default: local</span></div></li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="d3" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h2 id="d3" class="t28">What you get back</h2></div>
	<ul class="sets"><li><div class="set"><code>findings</code><p>The number of findings.</p></div></li><li><div class="set"><code>task-completable</code><p>Whether someone using a screen reader could finish the task you named.</p></div></li><li><div class="set"><code>result-json</code><p>The full result, with the transcript behind every finding.</p></div></li><li><div class="set"><code>summary-md</code><p>The report, ready to read.</p></div></li></ul><p>The report also appears in the run’s job summary. Keep the result files with the upload step above, so you can check any finding later.</p>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap prose" aria-labelledby="d4" style="gap:var(--space-4)"><div class="sh"><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">05</span><h2 id="d4" class="t28">Good to know</h2></div>
	<ul class="rows"><li><h3>It runs on Windows</h3><p>It uses windows-2022, because NVDA only runs on Windows. GitHub provides the machine.</p></li><li><h3>Your build is safe</h3><p>Findings don’t fail your build unless you set fail-on.</p></li><li><h3>Use it where it counts</h3><p>Run it on the flows that matter, like checkout and sign-up, not on every commit. A run takes real screen reader time.</p></li></ul><p><a class="lnk2 solo" href="https://github.com/a11ign/a11ign/blob/main/docs/github-action.md">Every option, on GitHub</a></p>
	    </section></div>
	  </main>
</Page>
